      "html": "<ul><li>Type: Rosulate</li><li>Origin: Cultivar</li><li>Growth rate: Medium</li><li>Height: 20 - 30+ cm (average height after two months in the tank)</li><li>Light demand: Low</li><li>CO2: Low</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Echinodorus'Ozelot'(073FXL)/4521",
      "html": "<p>Echinodorus 'Ozelot' is a decorative hybrid between Echinodorus schluteri 'Leopard' and Echinodorus 'Barthii'. It grows 20-50 cm tall with a rosette 20-40 cm wide. The plant gets its name from the elliptical black spots on the red-brown leaves. The spots are darkest on the youngest leaves, and unlike many other spotted Echinodorus, 'Ozelot' retains its spots even at low light intensity. It is an undemanding plant and a good choice for beginners.</p>"
    }
  ],
